* Detection: chroot execution attempts
*
* Hypothesis:
*   In a containerised environment, chroot execution may indicate an attempt
*   to break out of filesystem isolation. Combined with elevated privileges
*   or CAP_SYS_CHROOT, it is a container escape primitive.
*
* Tuning notes:
*   - The system invokes chroot in normal background operation, so raw volume
*     here is not meaningful on its own. Baseline first.
*   - The interesting cases are chroot invoked by an unexpected user, from an
*     interactive shell, or inside a container that should not have the
*     capability at all.
*   - Correlate with container runtime logs to establish whether the calling
*     process was inside a container boundary.

index="splunk_data" "chroot"
